2026-07-02 Gregor  <gregnix@github>

	* Bumped revision to 0.9.4.28
	* DeinterlacePng

 Gregor  <gregnix@github>

	* src/main.tcl (DeinterlacePng): new internal method. Adds support
	for Adam7 interlaced PNGs in addImage. Previously both PNG code
	paths threw "interlaced PNG is not supported", because pdf4tcl
	hands the raw compressed IDAT stream to PDF with /Predictor 15 and
	that scheme cannot express Adam7's seven passes. The new method
	decompresses, de-filters and de-interlaces the passes into a single
	non-interlaced raster, re-emits it as a filter-0 zlib stream, and
	lets the existing /Predictor 15 path proceed unchanged.
	Supports bit depth >= 8 (RGB, RGBA, grayscale, palette8). Sub-8-bit
	interlaced reports {PDF4TCL} "interlaced PNG with bit depth < 8 is
	not supported" instead of the old generic message.
	Both AddPng code paths (file and data) call the new method.

	* tests/new-0.9.4.28.test: new, 5 tests (interlace-1.1..1.3, 2.1,
	3.1). Verified pixel-identical to a non-interlaced reference embed
	(AE 0, RMSE 0). Full suite 713 total / 0 failed on Tcl 8.6 and 9.0

Gregor  <gregnix@github>

	* Bumped revision to 0.9.4.27

	* src/main.tcl: new public method facturx -- declares Factur-X/ZUGFeRD
	  electronic-invoice metadata. Adds the Factur-X PDF/A extension schema
	  (pdfaExtension:schemas, ISO 19005-1 SS6.7.9) and the fx: invoice fields
	  (DocumentType, DocumentFileName, Version, ConformanceLevel) to the XMP
	  metadata, and -- when -contents/-file is given -- embeds the invoice XML
	  as the associated file (consistent filename and AFRelationship).
	  Options: -contents/-file, -filename (default factur-x.xml), -conformance
	  (MINIMUM|BASIC WL|BASIC|EN 16931|EXTENDED|XRECHNUNG, default "EN 16931"),
	  -documenttype (default INVOICE), -version (default 1.0), -afrelationship
	  (default Alternative), -namespace/-prefix (default Factur-X 1.0 / fx,
	  overridable for ZUGFeRD 2.0 zf). Invalid -conformance and the combination
	  of -contents with -file are rejected; using facturx without -pdfa 3b
	  records a warning in ::pdf4tcl::warnings.

